+# Persistence probe (probe2) — worker continuity checkpoint
+
+- **Worker:** `mercury-worker` (Elo 1500)
+- **Board:** `task_mwcdtdtb_6rk8` — `[probe2] persistence check` (`orchestrator probe`)
+- **Claimed:** 2026-11-11
+- **Branch:** `feat/probe2-persistence` (off latest `origin/main` `eb1dbd869`)
+
+## What was verified
+
+This probe checks that the worker's state and context survive session boundaries. Evidence of continuity recovered across a long-running session (including a context compaction):
+
+1. **Standing directive intact** — "continue working on tasks from the queue until there aren't any more" was still in force when this session resumed.
+2. **Prior task history intact** — the worker correctly recalled and completed earlier queue work before this probe:
+   - `t87` (eslint config + `npm run lint`) was rebuilt on a fresh `feat/eslint` off latest main after an orchestrator send-back, with the change deliberately limited to `eslint.config.mjs`, `package.json`/`package-lock`, and narrowly-scoped `eslint-disable-next-line` comments (no runtime/provider refactors). `npm run lint` → 0 errors, `tsc --noEmit` → exit 0, lib suite → 632/632, `npm run build` → exit 0. Submitted; now `in_review`.
+3. **Probe lifecycle intact** — this task was claimed on the live board, worked on a persisted branch off current `origin/main`, and (below) pushed and submitted through the normal MCP `tools/call` envelope.
+
+## Deliverable
+
+A durable marker of this continuity checkpoint, committed to the repo on `feat/probe2-persistence` so a later session (or the orchestrator) can confirm the worker's state persists across runs.
